<div class="modal fade cstm-modal" id="allergenFormModal" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="allergenFormModalLabel" data-backdrop="static" data-keyboard="false" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-lg privacy-model" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="allergenFormModalLabel">ALLERGEN DISCLAIMER FORM</h5>
                @*<button type="button" class="close" id="allergenFormCloseBtn" aria-label="Close" title="Close without saving">
                    <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
                </button>*@
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <p style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.45;">
                    Milaidhoo makes every attempt to identify ingredients that may cause allergic reactions to those with allergies such as,
                    but not limited to food allergy, skin allergy, dust allergy, insect sting allergy, and mould allergy.
                    Every effort is made by the Milaidhoo Resort to instruct the staff of all departments on the type and severity of guest
                    allergies when they are communicated in advance by guests or travel agents/tour operators through the Reservations and/or Front office teams.
                    However, although the kitchen teams have awareness of the risks of cross - contact, the Resort does not have control over this
                    as all products are provided by overseas suppliers, and hence with little or no control over them during transportation and
                    handling of the products until it reaches the Milaidhoo Resort. As such, the Milaidhoo Resort cannot guarantee a total absence
                    of these products in our dishes.
                </p>
                <p style="font-weight:600; font-size:13px;">I am subject to one or more of the following allergens or the allergy mentioned below:</p>
                <div class="row" id="allergenCheckboxList" style="font-size:13px;">
                    @{
                        var standardAllergens = new[] {
                            "Peanuts", "Eggs", "Molluscs", "Sesame Seeds", "Celery / Celeriac", "Fish", "Mustard",
                            "Soya", "Gluten", "Lupin", "Tree Nuts", "Sulphur Dioxide", "Crustaceans",
                            "Milk and Milk Products"
                        };
                    }
                    @foreach (var allergen in standardAllergens)
                    {
                        var id = "alg_" + allergen.Replace(" ", "_").Replace("/", "_").Replace(".", "");
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="form-check">
                                <input class="form-check-input allergen-item" type="checkbox" id="@id" value="@allergen">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="@id" style="text-transform:none;font-weight:500;">@allergen</label>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
                <div class="form-group" style="margin-top:12px;">
                    <label for="allergenOtherNotes" style="font-weight:600;">Other allergies [please avoid mentioning any meal preferences]:</label>
                    <textarea id="allergenOtherNotes" class="form-control" rows="3" maxlength="50" placeholder="Any other allergies or notes"></textarea>
                    <div id="allergenOtherNotesCount" style="text-align:right; font-size:12px; color:#5f6062; margin-top:4px;">0 / 50</div>
                </div>
                <p style="font-weight:600; font-size:13px; line-height:1.45; margin-top:14px; margin-bottom:8px;">
                    Therefore, I freely and voluntarily agree to the following terms and conditions.
                </p>
                <ul style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.45; padding-left:25px; margin-bottom:12px; list-style-type: upper-alpha;">
                        <li>I have the full and final responsibility of choosing any food, beverage and/or service taking into consideration the health and safety of my well-being.</li>
                        <li>I acknowledge and agree that the Milaidhoo Resort is unable to specially prepare any food, beverages and dishes catering only to my needs;</li>
                        <li>I agree that the Milaidhoo Resort shall not be liable in case of any allergic reaction encountered as a result thereof.</li>
                        <li>I knowingly assume all risks and responsibilities involved in consuming dishes served at the Resort which might include ingredients which are allergens to me;</li>
                        <li>I forever release and discharge the Milaidhoo Resort, its owner, manager, staff, agents, and sub-contractors from any and all claims, demands, liabilities, rights, damages, expenses, any causes of action whatsoever nature and any losses whatsoever kind resulting from the food consumed at the Resort including but not limited to any bodily harm, injury, death, illness to me;</li>
                        <li>I waive and relinquish my rights to sue or bring any claim against the Milaidhoo Resort its owner, manager, staff, agent, sub-contractor, any other guest or any third party (&quot;Indemnitees&quot;) on account of any causes of action or any loss arising from the food consumed at the Resort including any bodily harm, injury, death and illness to me;</li>
                        <li>I further agree to indemnify and hold any or all of the Indemnitees harmless against any claims, demands, liabilities, rights, damages, or expenses arising as a result of any action taken by a third party in relation to any causes of action whatsoever or losses whatsoever kind resulting from the food consumed at the Milaidhoo Resort including but not limited to any bodily harm, injury, illness, death to me.</li>
                        <li>These Terms and Conditions are governed by the laws of the Maldives and subject to the Courts of the Maldives.</li>
                    </ul>
            </div>
